        <p>
    Your responses show clear thinking about how you measure leadership. You focus on developing others. You treat measurement as a tool for building capacity, not controlling outcomes. You understand that what you measure shapes what people pursue. You measure character, relationships, and agency on purpose. 
</p>
<p><strong>Your strengths:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>You measure others' development, not your own achievements</li>
    <li>You treat character, relationships, and agency as enduring metrics</li>
    <li>You see how measurement systems teach what matters most in leadership</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Growth opportunities:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>Share your measurement approach to help others build the same skills</li>
    <li>Look for chances to mentor others in enduring measurement</li>
    <li>Keep applying measurement principles to complex leadership situations</li>
</ul>
            
